WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:10.013
"No!" Julia cried as Heracles disappeared. She leaped forward and grabbed at the temple wall with her fingers.

2
00:00:10.014 --> 00:00:16.980
But there was nothing there except solid stone. The rift had disappeared too.

3
00:00:16.981 --> 00:00:24.364
She sank onto the floor, hardly believing what had just happened. Heracles was gone.

4
00:00:24.365 --> 00:00:30.002
And now Julia and Brody were trapped in ancient Greece . . . forever!

5
00:00:30.003 --> 00:00:37.028
Brody looked stunned too. "I can't believe that just happened," he murmured.

6
00:00:37.029 --> 00:00:44.792
Julia saw him staring at the wall behind her. "Whoa!" he cried. "What's going on?"

7
00:00:44.793 --> 00:00:51.361
Julia looked up. A faint spark of light was coming through a tiny crack in the wall.

8
00:00:51.362 --> 00:00:55.335
She stood and backed away, not daring to hope.

9
00:00:55.336 --> 00:00:59.587
Then a hand pushed through the wall, and another.

10
00:00:59.588 --> 00:01:04.151
Julia gasped. "Heracles!" she cried.

11
00:01:04.152 --> 00:01:09.624
They all stared at the wall in disbelief as the hands struggled to push the wall apart.

12
00:01:09.625 --> 00:01:13.765
Julia could hear Heracles grunting with effort.

13
00:01:13.766 --> 00:01:19.469
"He's doing it!" Brody shouted. "He's opening the rift back up!"

14
00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:25.031
"Impossible!" Hera moaned.

15
00:01:25.032 --> 00:01:34.697
It did seem impossible. But sure enough, Heracles was prying open the time passage that had just closed behind him!

16
00:01:34.698 --> 00:01:40.159
Soon the rift was wide enough for Heracles to wedge his upper body into it.

17
00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.862
Brody just stood there, staring in amazement.

18
00:01:43.863 --> 00:01:49.921
"Brody, help him!" Julia cried. "We have to get him through!"

19
00:01:49.922 --> 00:01:53.819
She grabbed Heracles' hand and pulled as hard as she could.

20
00:01:53.820 --> 00:02:00.120
For a moment nothing happened. Then Brody grabbed the hero's other hand.

21
00:02:00.121 --> 00:02:05.264
Heracles grimaced with pain as his broad shoulders scraped against the wall.

22
00:02:05.265 --> 00:02:10.444
"Don't pull me all the way through yet." He gasped out the words.

23
00:02:10.445 --> 00:02:14.174
"You have to get through the passage before it closes again!"

24
00:02:14.175 --> 00:02:21.189
Julia realized he was right. "But how can we fit through while you're in there too?" she asked.

25
00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:31.523
"Just give me a moment . . ." Heracles grunted and groaned, flexing the muscles in his powerful legs.

26
00:02:31.524 --> 00:02:36.034
He spread his legs apart, pushing the walls farther to the sides.

27
00:02:36.035 --> 00:02:42.416
Soon there was enough space—barely—for a person to duck between his legs.

28
00:02:42.417 --> 00:02:45.863
"Come on, Brody!" Julia cried.

29
00:02:45.864 --> 00:02:56.734
"Hurry," Heracles said through gritted teeth. "I don't know . . . how much longer . . . I can hold it open."

30
00:02:56.735 --> 00:03:04.089
"Thank you!" Julia cried, diving for the opening between Heracles' feet. "Thank you so much!"

31
00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:08.417
Brody still looked confused, so Julia grabbed his hand.

32
00:03:08.418 --> 00:03:13.636
She pulled him after her through Heracles' legs—and through the rift.

33
00:03:13.637 --> 00:03:22.942
Behind them, Julia heard Hera ranting. "You'll pay for defying me, Heracles!" she screamed.

34
00:03:22.943 --> 00:03:30.552
"Trust me, you won't have an easy day for the rest of your life, mark my . . ."

35
00:03:30.553 --> 00:03:36.208
[i@Snap!@i] Julia tumbled out of the rift onto the sidewalk near the school gym.

36
00:03:36.209 --> 00:03:40.611
"Ow," she said as her elbow scraped the pavement.

37
00:03:40.612 --> 00:03:43.703
Brody was lying on the ground beside her.

38
00:03:43.704 --> 00:03:49.953
He sat up and looked at the brick wall of the school building. Julia looked too.

39
00:03:49.954 --> 00:03:54.601
The wall appeared normal, with no sign of the rift.

40
00:03:54.602 --> 00:04:01.251
She stood up and gazed around. Actually, everything looked normal.

41
00:04:01.252 --> 00:04:09.855
Brody looked at Julia and grinned. "I guess we're not in ancient Greece anymore."

42
00:04:09.856 --> 00:04:16.529
A few days later, Julia pushed open the door to the school library and went inside.

43
00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:20.886
She had a math test the next day, and she needed to study.

44
00:04:20.887 --> 00:04:26.272
As she passed a table, she saw a copy of the school newspaper lying there.

45
00:04:26.273 --> 00:04:31.365
She picked it up, glancing at the photograph of Brody on the front page.

46
00:04:31.366 --> 00:04:35.755
Below the picture was the article she'd written about him.

47
00:04:35.756 --> 00:04:44.356
"Yo," a familiar voice said behind her. "Admiring your greatest article ever, huh?"

48
00:04:44.357 --> 00:04:52.305
Julia looked up. Brody stood there, grinning at her. A book was tucked under his arm.

49
00:04:52.306 --> 00:04:55.558
"What are you doing here?" she asked.

50
00:04:55.559 --> 00:04:59.158
"I didn't think you even knew where the library was!"

51
00:04:59.159 --> 00:05:08.186
"Ha-ha!" Brody laughed. "Good one!" Then he held up the book to show her. It was about ancient Greece.

52
00:05:08.187 --> 00:05:15.034
Julia raised an eyebrow. She looked around to make sure nobody was close enough to hear them.

53
00:05:15.035 --> 00:05:18.719
"Don't you know enough about that topic already?"

54
00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:23.786
Brody shrugged. "You can always learn more about stuff, right?

55
00:05:23.787 --> 00:05:27.172
Anyway, some of those myths you told me were interesting."

56
00:05:27.173 --> 00:05:30.518
He stuck the book in his backpack.

57
00:05:30.519 --> 00:05:34.780
"And I want to find out more about what happens to Heracles later."

58
00:05:34.781 --> 00:05:40.509
Julia nodded. She couldn't stop thinking about Heracles herself.

59
00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:46.295
He was going to have a hard time with Hera; Julia knew that from the myths she'd read.

60
00:05:46.296 --> 00:05:51.386
Had Julia and Brody made things even worse for him? She hoped not.

61
00:05:51.387 --> 00:05:55.683
But she supposed they'd never find out for sure.

62
00:05:55.684 --> 00:06:01.634
"We've only been back for a few days, but it seems like longer, doesn't it?" she said.

63
00:06:01.635 --> 00:06:08.142
"Sort of," Brody replied. "It's weird how no time passed while we were gone."

64
00:06:08.143 --> 00:06:10.356
Julia nodded again.

65
00:06:10.357 --> 00:06:20.211
When they'd returned through the rift, she and Brody had quickly figured out that only a few seconds had passed in their time while they were away.

66
00:06:20.212 --> 00:06:25.645
That was definitely strange, because they'd been in ancient Greece for a couple of weeks.

67
00:06:25.646 --> 00:06:30.250
So many things had happened to the two of them during those weeks!

68
00:06:30.251 --> 00:06:35.749
But now that they were back in their own time, it was as if nothing had changed.

69
00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:41.031
She shrugged. "I guess that's how time travel works. Who knew?"

70
00:06:41.032 --> 00:06:49.199
Just then several popular kids came into the library. They spotted Brody and waved.

71
00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:53.362
Suddenly one of the girls noticed Julia standing there.

72
00:06:53.363 --> 00:07:02.455
"Hi, Julia!" she said, hurrying over. "I've been meaning to tell you, I really like your article about Brody."

73
00:07:02.456 --> 00:07:05.557
"Thanks," Julia said shyly.

74
00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:08.954
"Julia?" The other girl hurried over too.

75
00:07:08.955 --> 00:07:16.349
"I'm having a party this weekend. It's Saturday night at eight. I hope you can come."

76
00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:21.388
"Yeah, Julia, you should go," Brody put in. "I'll be there."

77
00:07:21.389 --> 00:07:28.356
"Thanks," Julia said. "I . . . um . . . I think I can probably make it."

78
00:07:28.357 --> 00:07:31.762
"Great!" The girl smiled.

79
00:07:31.763 --> 00:07:38.085
Julia was smiling too as the girls walked away. She was wrong.

80
00:07:38.086 --> 00:07:45.893
Some things had changed since she and Brody traveled to ancient Greece!

